<form autocomplete="off">
    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Send Crew to Combat Initiative, not Vehicle</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleCombatCrewMode" {{checked vehicleCombatCrewMode}}>
        <p class="notes">When selected, adding a vehicle to combat initiative will search its Cargo/Crew and attempt to add them to combat initiative. If it does not find a match, choose whether to generate a placeholder or only use matched sidebar actors.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Crew Initiative Matching</label>
        <div class="form-fields">
            <select name="vehicleCrewMatchMode">
                {{#each crewMatchModes}}
                <option value="{{value}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{label}}</option>
                {{/each}}
            </select>
        </div>
        <p class="notes"><strong>Match + Generate Actors:</strong> matches actors from the sidebar in the world and adds them to initiative order under the vessel. It also generates crew members that have no sidebar actor but do have a name, using a blank token.</p>
        <p class="notes"><strong>Match Actors Only:</strong> matches actors from the sidebar, but omits anyone who does not have a sidebar actor.</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Combat Order Display</label>
        <div class="form-fields">
            <select name="vehicleCombatDisplayMode">
                {{#each displayModes}}
                <option value="{{value}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{label}}</option>
                {{/each}}
            </select>
        </div>
        <p class="notes">Full shows vessel and crew portraits with Vessel / Crew names. Simple shows the crew portrait with a small ship badge overlay.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Do not show photos for non matched crew</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleCombatHideUnmatchedCrewPhotos" {{checked vehicleCombatHideUnmatchedCrewPhotos}}>
        <p class="notes">Generated crew still appear in the combat order by name, but their placeholder portrait is hidden.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Ship Badge Icon</label>
        <div class="form-fields">
            <input type="text" name="vehicleCombatShipIcon" value="{{vehicleCombatShipIcon}}">
            <button type="button" data-action="browse-ship-icon" title="Browse image files">
                <i class="fas fa-folder-open"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>FSA Manages Combat Speed</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleCombatSpeedManaged" {{checked vehicleCombatSpeedManaged}}>
        <p class="notes">Track and enforce vehicle movement during active combat rounds.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Shared Movement</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleCombatSharedMovement" {{checked vehicleCombatSharedMovement}}>
        <p class="notes">At the start of each round, the vehicle gains movement equal to its Speed. On any crew member's turn, that character may spend part of the vehicle's remaining movement. The total movement spent by all crew members cannot exceed the vehicle's Speed before the next round.</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Enable Vehicle Operations</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleOpsEnabled" {{checked vehicleOpsEnabled}}>
        <p class="notes">Enable Full Speed Ahead's vehicle operation logic for ship items, damage calculation, fuel scooping, mining damage, scans, repair, heat sinks, and cargo failure tools.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Show GM FSA Floating Menu</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleOpsShowFloatingMenuGM" {{checked vehicleOpsShowFloatingMenuGM}}>
        <p class="notes">Show the draggable FSA floating operations menu and vehicle operations scene-control button to the GM.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Show FSA Floating Menu to Players</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleOpsShowFloatingMenuPlayers" {{checked vehicleOpsShowFloatingMenuPlayers}}>
        <p class="notes">Show the draggable FSA floating operations menu and vehicle operations scene-control button to non-GM users.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Fallback Repair Cost Per Module HP</label>
        <input type="number" name="vehicleOpsRepairCostPerHp" value="{{vehicleOpsRepairCostPerHp}}" min="0" step="1">
        <p class="notes">Used when TradeHub is unavailable or does not expose a repair HP cost.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Fallback Repair Cost Per Shield HP</label>
        <input type="number" name="vehicleOpsRepairCostPerShieldPoint" value="{{vehicleOpsRepairCostPerShieldPoint}}" min="0" step="1">
        <p class="notes">Used when TradeHub is unavailable or does not expose a shield repair HP cost.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Ship Long Rest Upkeep Percentage</label>
        <input type="number" name="vehicleOpsShipUpkeepPercent" value="{{vehicleOpsShipUpkeepPercent}}" min="0" step="0.01">
        <p class="notes">Percentage of total ship cost billed for each vehicle long rest. Enter 0.2 for 0.2%, 2 for 2%, etc. When TradeHub Markets exposes this setting, FSA reads and writes TradeHub's value.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Insurance Company Name</label>
        <input type="text" name="vehicleOpsInsuranceCompanyName" value="{{vehicleOpsInsuranceCompanyName}}" autocomplete="off">
        <p class="notes">Displayed wherever vehicle insurance appears. Internal saved coverage remains compatible with existing insured ships.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Insurance Premium Percentage</label>
        <input type="number" name="vehicleOpsGlaxonPremiumPercent" value="{{vehicleOpsGlaxonPremiumPercent}}" min="0" step="0.01">
        <p class="notes">Percentage of full repair value billed as the insured long-rest premium. When TradeHub Markets exposes an insurance premium setting or calculator, FSA reads and writes that shared value.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Require Insurance Confirmation Code</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleOpsInsuranceCodeRequired" {{checked vehicleOpsInsuranceCodeRequired}}>
        <p class="notes">When enabled, subscribing to vehicle insurance requires a confirmation code from an NPC representative.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Insurance Confirmation Code</label>
        <input type="text" name="vehicleOpsInsuranceConfirmationCode" value="{{vehicleOpsInsuranceConfirmationCode}}" autocomplete="off">
        <p class="notes">Players must enter this exact code after clicking Insure My Vehicle before new coverage can be activated. Cancelling existing coverage does not require the code.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Use TokenMagic Damage Bursts</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleOpsTokenMagicDamage" {{checked vehicleOpsTokenMagicDamage}}>
        <p class="notes">If TokenMagic FX is installed, show splash damage filters when vehicle modules take damage.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Use Item Piles for Cargo Jettison</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleOpsItemPilesJettison" {{checked vehicleOpsItemPilesJettison}}>
        <p class="notes">If Item Piles is installed, create cargo piles near the vehicle when Cargo Bay failure jettisons cargo.</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <div class="form-group">
        <label>Debug Logging</label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="vehicleCombatDebug" {{checked vehicleCombatDebug}}>
    </div>

    <footer class="sheet-footer flexrow">
        <button type="submit">
            <i class="fas fa-save"></i> Save
        </button>
    </footer>
</form>
